# BACKEND Explaination 

# Backend Overview (Short)

This backend is a FastAPI service for a credit-risk assistant. It supports RAG chat, tabular ML predictions, scenario simulation, SHAP explainability, speech-to-text, ingestion, and lightweight observability.

## Core Components

- API gateway: app.py (monolith entrypoint).
- RAG pipeline: rag_pipeline.py (retrieve -> generate -> postprocess).
- LLM runtime: model_loader.py (local Transformers) + model_server_client.py (optional external model server).
- Tabular scoring: ml_predict.py (LR/CatBoost/NN) + feature_store.py (shared feature contract).
- Vector store: chroma_loader.py (Chroma + E5 embeddings).
- Speech-to-text: speech_to_text.py (Whisper).
- Observability: observability.py + event_bus.py (traces + events).
- Job queue: job_queue.py (in-process async jobs).

## Key Flows (High Level)

RAG chat
1) /query or /stream receives a question
2) rag_pipeline.py retrieves chunks from Chroma
3) model_loader.py (or model server) generates the answer
4) response includes answer + retrieved context

Prediction
1) /predict validates features (Pydantic)
2) ml_predict.py scores all available models
3) response includes PD, grade, decision, and top features

Scenario simulation
1) /scenario merges baseline + overrides
2) each scenario is scored via ml_predict.py
3) response includes deltas and derived metrics

Ingestion
1) /ingest chunks incoming text
2) chunks are embedded and added to Chroma

Speech-to-text
1) /transcribe accepts WAV
2) whisper-medium transcribes audio to text

## Deployment Modes

Single service (default)
- Run app.py directly for all features.

Split services (optional)
- services/api_gateway.py (port 8000)
- services/inference_service.py (port 8011)
- services/retrieval_service.py (port 8012)
- services/tabular_scoring_service.py (port 8013)

## Storage and Models

- Vector DB: chroma_db/ (Chroma persistent store)
- LLMs: model/llama-1b and model/llama-3b
- Tabular ML: ML_Model/ (joblib/pickle artifacts)

## Useful Environment Flags

- SKIP_STARTUP_LOAD=1 to skip heavy startup loads
- LLM_MODEL_SERVER_URL to use external vLLM/TGI for generation
- TABULAR_SCORING_SERVICE_URL to delegate scoring to the split service
- OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT to send events to OpenTelemetry

## What To Read First

- app.py: routes and orchestration
- rag_pipeline.py: retrieval + generation logic
- ml_predict.py: ML scoring and SHAP
- feature_store.py: canonical feature contract
